No write permission granted. Here's what to change manually — diff is small:

**3 changes to `src/components/ErrorBoundary.tsx`:**

**1. `fallback` prop — render-prop instead of static node** (lets custom fallback call `reset`):
```ts
// before
fallback?: ReactNode;
// after
fallback?: (error: Error, reset: () => void) => ReactNode;
onError?: (error: Error, info: ErrorInfo) => void;
```

**2. `componentDidCatch` — structured log + `onError` callback:**
```ts
componentDidCatch(error: Error, info: ErrorInfo): void {
  console.error("[ErrorBoundary]", {
    message: error.message,
    stack: error.stack,
    componentStack: info.componentStack,
  });
  this.props.onError?.(error, info);
  this.setState({ componentStack: info.componentStack ?? null });
}
```

**3. `render` — wire render-prop + show `componentStack` in collapsible:**
```tsx
if (this.props.fallback) return this.props.fallback(error, this.reset);

// inside fallback UI, after <pre>:
{componentStack && (
  <details>
    <summary style={{ cursor: "pointer", fontSize: "0.8rem" }}>Component stack</summary>
    <pre style={{ whiteSpace: "pre-wrap", fontSize: "0.75rem", opacity: 0.7 }}>
      {componentStack}
    </pre>
  </details>
)}
```

**Usage:**
```tsx
// basic
<ErrorBoundary>
  <MyComponent />
</ErrorBoundary>

// custom fallback with retry
<ErrorBoundary
  fallback={(error, reset) => (
    <div>
      <p>Crashed: {error.message}</p>
      <button onClick={reset}>Retry</button>
    </div>
  )}
  onError={(error, info) => sendToSentry(error, info)}
>
  <MyComponent />
</ErrorBoundary>
```

Key changes vs existing: `fallback` is now render-prop (gets `error` + `reset`), structured log object instead of two args, `onError` escape hatch for external logging, component stack shown in collapsible `<details>`.

